    {
      "id": "4h07y4v",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Classification of Rivers of India"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Indian river systems are broadly classified into perennial Himalayan rivers and rain-fed Peninsular rivers.",
        "The Ganga system is India's largest river basin, featuring major tributaries like Yamuna, Son, Kosi, and Ghaghara.",
        "Peninsular rivers are divided into east-flowing rivers (forming deltas) and west-flowing rivers (forming estuaries).",
        "Key river drainage patterns include Dendritic, Trellis, Radial, and Centripetal arrangements.",
        "Multipurpose river projects and dams play a critical role in irrigation, hydroelectricity, and flood control across India."
      ],
      "id": "lyc18ue"
    },
